  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Fig 15, 'Maturity-based architecture: moving from SCISMM Level 3 to Level 4'. The digital health supply chain enterprise has shared services (facility, product and supplier registries) and data services (supply chain reports, data warehouse, track and trace, product verification) above an interoperability layer (authentication, encryption, transformation, orchestration, validation, translation), which connects eight health supply chain information systems: forecasting and planning, order, warehouse and cold chain management, procurement, supplier and contract management, transportation management and dispensing.",
